title: Cross-parachain source discovery (governance-gated, version-gated)

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Node Dev]
    description: |
      Adds cross-parachain source discovery as a standalone, governance-gated, version-gated layer.
      A parachain can be told on-chain, via governance
      (`cumulus-pallet-source-discovery::set_source_genesis`, bounded by `MaxSources`), how to reach
      another parachain's collators; its node then resolves that source's peers over the relay-chain
      DHT (RFC-0008 `/paranode`) using `cumulus-client-source-discovery`, keeping a shared
      `PeerRegistry` that a higher layer (e.g. speculative messaging) can consume. No messaging or
      fetch is involved — this is only the discovery substrate.

      Version-gated and opt-in: a runtime without `SourceDiscoveryApi`, or with no configured
      source, behaves exactly as before. Serving collators additionally advertise under a
      capability-scoped DHT provider key (opt-in via the `--spec-msg-serve` collator flag) so
      discovery resolves only serving collators, sidestepping the closest-K dilution of the plain
      RFC-0008 key.

crates:
  - name: cumulus-primitives-source-discovery
    bump: major
  - name: cumulus-pallet-source-discovery
    bump: major
  - name: cumulus-client-source-discovery
    bump: major
  - name: cumulus-client-bootnodes
    bump: major
  - name: cumulus-client-cli
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
    bump: patch
  - name: penpal-runtime
    bump: minor
